@TheLeoP, I've finally found enough determination to touch tree-sitter testing :sweat_smile: Both 'mini.ai' and 'mini.surround' now use real tree-sitter parser and `vim.treesitter` (which allowed to find issues on Nightly, by the way).

If you still have time and aspiration to have this functionality (which is *very* welcome), it requires conflict resolution and different testing. I'd also appreciate if there is a similar change to 'mini.surround' and its `gen_spec.input.treesitter()`, as it should have as much in common as `gen_spec.treesitter()` from 'mini.ai'.

If it is a "no" to any of these, I'd completely understand and will do this myself (hopefully, again, by the end of this week).
